      "text": "And what we have done with artificial intelligence is that we have been able to make sure that our data sets are accessible to people in different places, in different systems. And that has enhanced accessibility to information. But I need to say that the access to information hasn't been without challenges. There are challenges of cultural and social values that sometimes artificial intelligence doesn't respect. And that is caused a little discomfort in some of our people. But on the main, what we have seen is benefiting the people from artificial intelligence, is that number one, it is helping them access automated information. So automated information is easier in terms of each summation for people. So if you have got different data sets and you want to find information which is useful",
